    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOI7W0xc7vEdM0",
      "title": "chainsmeta: tolerate SystemConfig 4.0.0 removed getters",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 1799,
      "body": "SystemConfig 4.0.0 (op-contracts v8.0.0, https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/21641) removes the `batchInbox()`, `startBlock()`, `BATCH_INBOX_SLOT()`, and `START_BLOCK_SLOT()` getters that the chainsmeta systemconfig ingest calls on every chain. Chains upgrade at different times, so the ingest must tolerate both versions indefinitely.\n\nThe pipeline already treats per-method reverts as None (that is how `operatorFeeScalar` and friends work on not-yet-upgraded chains), so reverts from removed getters were already handled. The actual gap: some nodes answer an `eth_call` to a removed method with an empty `0x` result instead of a revert, which previously produced garbage for address fields (`\"0x0x\"`) or raised for int fields. This PR treats an empty result the same as a revert, marks the two slot annotations `Optional`, and adds a test covering both failure shapes against a 4.0.0 SystemConfig.\n\nNo SQL changes — the ClickHouse columns are already `Nullable`. Historical rows keep their values; post-upgrade rows get NULL for the removed fields.\n\nTests: `uv run pytest tests/op_analytics/datasources/chainsmeta/ -v` → 19 passed; mypy and ruff clean.\n\nRelated PRs: https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/21641 (contracts), https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/specs/pull/922 (spec), https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/pull/1492 (upgrade tooling), the dev-docs edit rides along in the monorepo PR. Context: ethereum-optimism/optimism#21614.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-analytics",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-08T00:56:17Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 85,
      "deletions": 2
    }
